{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment-domain","title":"def:pet-ch5-segment-domain","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.md","line":1294,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex#def:pet-ch5-segment-domain","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-hopf-rinow]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","label":"def:pet-ch5-segment-domain","line":2773,"source":"\\begin{definition}[segment domain and its star interior]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch5-segment-domain}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0232,petersen:page-0233}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch5-segment, thm:pet-ch5-hopf-rinow}\n\n  For a complete $(M,g)$ and $p\\in M$, the \\emph{segment domain} is\n  $\\operatorname{seg}(p)=\\{v\\in T_pM\\mid\\exp_p(tv):[0,1]\\to M\\text{ is a segment}\\}$,\n  a closed star-shaped set with $M=\\exp_p(\\operatorname{seg}(p))$ (by\n  \\cref{thm:pet-ch5-hopf-rinow}). Its \\emph{star interior} is\n  $\\operatorname{seg}^0(p)=\\{sv\\mid s\\in[0,1),\\,v\\in\\operatorname{seg}(p)\\}$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[segment domain and its star interior] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368352d7365676d656e742d646f6d61696e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0232, petersen:page-0233</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23def%3Apet-ch5-segment\">↗ def:pet-ch5-segmen